                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e9fd4726-8573-3c5f-b5a7-464e6206f527",
                        "entry_id": "b4fd32a5-112c-3b3d-9273-3b9c0ad6eb44",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To formulate again or differently."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "970838e8-d3c4-4071-912c-d7056c81a236",
                                "sense_id": "e9fd4726-8573-3c5f-b5a7-464e6206f527",
                                "text": "Some soft drinks have been reformulated to include less sugar."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc649332-d268-456a-a265-a0180315352f",
                                "sense_id": "e9fd4726-8573-3c5f-b5a7-464e6206f527",
                                "text": "A narrative circulates at Mitchell, Hall about a naive young employee who, in his eagerness to be creative, \"reinvents the wheel,\" devoting so many hours reformulating work that has already been done that he drives himself into a nervous breakdown."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14181384-752e-469a-942f-bbc6e2ce9e13",
                                "sense_id": "e9fd4726-8573-3c5f-b5a7-464e6206f527",
                                "text": "In musicals, when they are not unabashedly revivals, the assumption seems to be all we need do is find appropriate chunks of recent, or not-so-recent, history and cleverly reformulate them. Remakes, re-dos, sequels, prequels, and postquels are all the rage in films, TV, and on the stage."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86e793a9-87aa-4653-b5c9-b43332213ebe",
                                "sense_id": "e9fd4726-8573-3c5f-b5a7-464e6206f527",
                                "text": "In the present paper this criterion is reformulated in terms of pseudotensorial invariants of the form.."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7b5f8dfe-0bd1-4572-b3d4-21b3ccb0ef20",
                                "sense_id": "e9fd4726-8573-3c5f-b5a7-464e6206f527",
                                "text": "He states and restates, formulates and reformulates, refines and rerefines."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "42fc4746-abec-47a5-ac40-ea27b5773618",
                                "sense_id": "e9fd4726-8573-3c5f-b5a7-464e6206f527",
                                "text": "\"This is now called Skimpflation, which means a manufacturer has reformulated one of its products, usually with cheaper ingredients,\" says Dworsky, a former Massachusetts Assistant Attorney General in consumer protection."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
